 "text": "Government / Pike County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nPike County, Indiana\nSearch\nSubmit\nMenu\nHome\nGovernment  Boards & Commissions\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nCounty Officials  Assessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nClerk's Office\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nSheriff's Office\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nDepartments  Health Department\nHighway Department\nParks & Recreation Department\nProbation Department\nPurdue Extension, Pike Co.\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSolid Waste Department\nVeteran's Services Office\nPublic Safety  E911\nEMA\nEMS\nSheriff's Office\nTaxes\nCommunity\nHow Do I?  Browse County Staff\nFind an Event\nFind a Location\nFind a Service\nView FAQs\nView a Slideshow\nVisit the Meeting Center\nFind a Document  Agendas\nBreaking News\nForms & Applications\nMinutes\nNews & Notices\nUseful Links\nStart Content\nGovernment\nHome\nGovernment\nThe following list contains links to town departments, elected officials and their contact information.\nYou might also be interested in:\nBoards and Commissions\nMeeting Center\nElected Officials\nAssessor's Office\n(812) 354-6584\nAuditor's Office\nThe County Council meets monthly on the 2nd Tuesday at 8:30 a.m. in the Pike County Courthouse Auditorium.\n(812) 354-6451\n\nClerk's Office\n(812) 354-6025\n\nCounty Commissioners\n(812) 354-8448\nCounty Council\n(812) 354-6451\nPrides Creek Conservancy District\n(812) 354-8881\n\nProsecutor's Office\n(812) 354-8761\nRecorder's Office\n(812) 354-6747\nSeptic Application\nSheriff's Office\nSurveyor\nTreasurer's Office\n(812) 354-6363\n\nDepartments\nChamber of Commerce\nE911\n(812) 354-6024\nEMS\n(812) 354-8796\nEconomic Development Corporation\n(812) 354-2271\n\nEmergency Management\n(812) 354-6776\n\nHealth Department\n(812) 354-8797\nHighway Department\n(812) 354-9743\n\nParks and Recreation Department\n(812) 354-6798\n\nPike County Redevelopment Commission\nThe Pike County Redevelopment Commission was created by IC 36-7-14 & IC 36-7-25 (collectively called the \"Act\"). The Act states the clearance, planning, replanning, redevelopment or economic development of blighted areas and economic development areas are public uses and purposes for which public money may be spent and private property may be acquired. The commission is comprised of a 5 person board and affords the county a maximum opportunity for rehabilitation, redevelopment or economic development opf areas by private enterprise.\nProbation Department\n(812) 354-8034\nPurdue Extension, Pike Co.\nSoil & Water Conservation District\n(812) 354-6120 x 3\nSolid Waste Department\n(812) 354-2924\n\nSummer Training\nSurveyor\n(812) 354-9736\n\nVeterans Services Office\n(812) 354-6245\nOnline Payments\nStaff Directory\nPublic Meetings\nForms & Applications\nEmployment\n© 2026 Pike County, Indiana\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCore Business Technologies",
